## Summary

submit() closes the modal and clears the form, then awaits refreshMemories()/refreshStats() inside the same try block. If either refresh rejects after api.remember succeeded, control jumps to catch and shows an error toast — the user believes the memory was NOT saved and retypes it, creating a duplicate. The save already succeeded and the form was cleared, so the error is also mis-attributed.

## Evidence

- **File**: `src/components/QuickAdd.tsx` (lines 40-50)

```
setContent(""); setTags(""); setOpen(false);
await refreshMemories();
await refreshStats();
showToast({ kind: "ok", text: "Remembered" });
} catch (e) {
  showToast({ kind: "err", text: String(e) }); // fires even though remember() succeeded
```

## Suggested fix

Show the success toast immediately after api.remember resolves; move refreshes outside the try.

