## Summary

When enqueue() finds g.running it sets g.queued=true and returns WITHOUT sending on the channel; the Full branch of try_send does the same. Nothing ever reads g.queued to synthesize a follow-up job: worker only clears the flag when it dequeues its next channel message, and run_once ignores it. A user clicking 'consolidate now' while a run is in flight loses the request entirely, and get_status() reports queued=true / next_run_in_secs=0 indefinitely. io.rs implements the correct re-run pattern; scheduler.rs does not.

## Evidence

- **File**: `src-tauri/src/scheduler.rs` (lines 102-107,120-124)

```
if g.running {
    // Coalesce: one manual job is enough while another runs. Mark queued.
    g.queued = true;
    return Ok(());
}
```

## Suggested fix

Always try_send (capacity 8 buffers fine), or have worker after each run_once re-check g.queued and enqueue a ManualJob before blocking on recv().

