## Summary

Rust RecallExplanation serializes an additional applied_boosts object (RankingBoosts: content_matches, tag_matches, path_matches, language_match, multiplier, importance_boost) on every ExplainedMemory from recall_explain. types.ts has neither the field nor the struct, so the TS contract is incomplete and does not match serde output field-by-field.

## Evidence

- **File**: `src/lib/types.ts` (lines 34-39)

```
export interface RecallExplanation {
  vector_rank: number | null;
  fts_rank: number | null;
  matched_terms: string[];
  feedback_boost: number;
}  // Rust also has applied_boosts: RankingBoosts
```

## Suggested fix

Add applied_boosts: RankingBoosts to RecallExplanation and define the RankingBoosts interface mirroring recall.rs:20-27.

