## Summary

release.md claims the release script 'refuses to create a tag if it already exists locally or on the remote'. release.mjs only runs git rev-parse locally; no ls-remote check. With a remote-only tag the script proceeds, creates local tag, then fails at push — leaving stray local tag, contrary to docs. Line 7 also says changes must be pushed to main, but script uses whatever branch is current.

## Evidence

- **File**: `docs/release.md` (lines 104-104)

```
try {
  git(`rev-parse ${tag}`);
  tagExists = true;
} catch { /* Tag doesn't exist */ }
```

## Suggested fix

Add remote check (git ls-remote --tags origin ${tag}) before creating; align doc wording with actual enforcement.

