Found during a full-codebase audit (pass 2 · slice `build-ci`). **Kind:** bug · **Severity:** low

## Summary

format_context_block returns '<biTurboContext>no relevant memories</biTurboContext>' for the empty case, but non-empty results are wrapped in '<ctx>...</ctx>'. INSTRUCTIONS.md (and the server's own initialize instructions) tell agents to treat the '<biTurboContext>' block as authoritative context — agents matching that literal marker will never find it on successful recalls, only on empty ones. The documented contract and the actual output tag disagree.

## Evidence

- **File**: `src-tauri/src/mcp.rs` (lines 496-537)

```
if hits.is_empty() {
        return "<biTurboContext>no relevant memories</biTurboContext>".into();
    }
    ...
    let mut s = String::from("<ctx>\n");
    ... s.push_str("</ctx>");
```

## Suggested fix

Use one marker everywhere (<biTurboContext>) or update INSTRUCTIONS.md/initialize instructions to match <ctx>.

